cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NeoPhylo: Learn how phylogenetic trees are built — step by step, in your browser"
abstract: "A browser-based teaching tool for distance-based phylogenetics of
  DNA and protein sequences. Step through Neighbor-Joining and UPGMA one join
  at a time, compare p, Kimura and JTT distances (matching PHYLIP protdist),
  simulate sequence evolution on a known tree, and work with real data in
  guided lessons and a sandbox that reads and writes PHYLIP formats."
version: 1.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Khan"
    given-names: "Dorrabb"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/dorrabbkhan/NeoPhylo"
url: "https://neophylo.netlify.app"
date-released: 2026-10-19
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - neighbor-joining
  - UPGMA
  - distance methods
  - science education
  - interactive teaching
  - protein evolution
  - JTT
  - PHYLIP
